tive Study of Chronic Care Model Implementation</article-title><source>Ann Fam Med</source><year>2006</year><volume>4</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>317</fpage><lpage>326</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16868235</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1370/afm.570</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Leykum</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Pugh</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Lawrence</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Parchman</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Noel</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Cornell</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>McDaniel</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Organizational interventions employing principles of complexity science have improved outcomes for patients with Type II diabetes</article-title><source>Implementation Science</source><year>2007</year><volume>2</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>28</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17725834</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1748-5908-2-28</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Chronic Disease and Illness Care: Additional Principles of Family Medicine are needed to address ongoing health system redesign</article-title><source>Can Fam Physician</source><year>2007</year><volume>53</volume><issue>12</issue><fpage>2086</fpage><lpage>2091</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18077734</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Von Korff</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gruman</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Schaefer</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Curry</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Wagner</surname><given-names>EH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Collaborative Management of Chronic Illness</article-title><source>Ann Intern Med</source><year>1997</year><volume>127</volume><issue>12</issue><fpage>1097</fpage><lpage>1102</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9412313</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Britt</surname><given-names>HC</given-names></name><name><surname>Harrison</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Miller</surname><given-names>GC</given-names></name><name><surname>Knox</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prevalence and patterns of multimorbidity in Australia</article-title><source>Med J Aust</source><year>2008</year><volume>189</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>72</fpage><lpage>77</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18637770</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Battersby</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Harvey</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Mills</surname><given-names>PD</given-names></name><name><surname>Kalucy</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Pols</surname><given-names>RG</given-names></name><name><surname>Frith</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>McDonald</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Esterman</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsourtos</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Donato</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>SA HealthPlus: a controlled trial of a statewide application of a generic model of chronic illness care</article-ti